YouthChain: Sierra Leone’s AI + Blockchain Employment Passport
1. Problem Statement

Youth in Sierra Leone face high unemployment and underemployment. Many young people have skills—formal, informal, or self-taught—but lack verifiable proof that employers and government agencies can trust. Traditional CVs are easy to fake, and many skills aren’t captured at all. As a result, youth are excluded from real jobs, training programs, and opportunities.

2. Solution: YouthChain

YouthChain is a digital platform that creates a secure, blockchain-backed “employment passport” for young people.

AI Matching Engine: Uses AI to recommend jobs, freelance gigs, or training opportunities based on skills, interests, and local demand.

Blockchain Credentials: Every completed training, internship, or job is stored on blockchain as a tamper-proof credential, forming a digital work history.

Youth Passport App: Youth have a personal digital wallet (mobile/web) showing verified skills and job matches.

Employer/Agency Portal: Employers, NGOs, and government programs can instantly verify candidates without paperwork delays.

3. Why It’s Different

Not just a job board → It creates a trust layer with blockchain verification.

Not just skills training → It connects youth to real jobs while capturing credentials.

Not just blockchain hype → Combined with AI matching, it directly solves a human problem: getting youth into work.

4. Impact (Aligned with Big Five Agenda)

Youth Employment Scheme (YES!): Gives youth a direct, verifiable path into jobs.

Public Service Transformation: Supports digital ID for employment and training.

Feed Salone & Education: Farmers and students can be issued blockchain credentials for training and participation in programs.

Scalability: Can expand into agriculture, health, and education sectors.

5. Technology Stack (Prototype Plan)

Frontend: Flutter app (mobile + web).

AI: Recommendation engine using GPT/transformer models for job matching.

Blockchain: Hyperledger or Ethereum testnet for credential issuance.

Backend: Flask/Django API + PostgreSQL for data.

Integration: Node-RED for quick dashboards and visualization.

6. Roadmap for Hackathon

Phase 1 – Bootcamp:

Finalize MVP design and datasets (mock job postings + youth profiles).

Build AI job-matching demo.

Phase 2 – Hackathon:

Demo a live Flutter app: register user → AI recommends a job → blockchain issues credential.

Show government/NGO portal verifying credentials.

Pitch the impact with live demo + mock success story.

